- [Ma-kun] Why are you flustered?

252
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:14,163
- Are you nervous?
- He's already losing it.

253
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,582
- [Hikaru] That's cute.
- [Ma-kun] You're funny.

254
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:18,167
- [Assun] Boy.
- So, are you called Bo?

255
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,002
That's right. My type of woman is…

256
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,503
BO (27)
FUKUOKA - COMMERCIAL PAINTER

257
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:23,839
Well, as long as she has
a strong sense of self.

258
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,508
- Oh!
- [Bo] Nice to meet you.

259
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:27,718
RURU (26)
TOKYO - MODEL

260
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:29,178
My name is Ruru.

261
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:30,679
I work as a model.

262
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:34,850
I like guys who are manly
and have nice tattoos. [giggles]

263
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:36,852
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice.

264
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:40,314
My nickname is Tai-chan.

265
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:41,857
TAI-CHAN (22)
TOKYO - HAIRSTYLIST

266
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,567
I'm a hairstylist.

267
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,611
- Ooh!
- So unexpected!

268
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:46,695
[Tai-chan] I'm 22.

269
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:49,531
And I'd say
my type of girl is a flashy girl.

270
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:50,449
[Ruru] Oh.

271
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:52,368
My name is Hikaru. Nice to meet you.

272
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:53,619
HIKARU (23)
KANAGAWA - HOSTESS

273
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:55,037
I'm 23 years old.

274
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,122
And I'm a sucker for a gentleman.

275
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,750
- Nice to meet you.
- [Ari] Yeah!

276
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:03,504
Gentleman, huh?

277
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:05,923
[boy on PA] <i>Attention.</i>

278
00:16:06,006 --> 00:16:07,716
<i>Please show your true selves,</i>

279
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,009
<i>face your past,</i>

280
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:12,096
<i>and learn about love with all your might.</i>

281
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:14,682
<i>If you work hard,</i>
<i>a new version of yourselves</i>

282
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:17,476
<i>will be waiting for you</i>
<i>at the end of this journey.</i>

283
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:20,604
<i>Please make sure you follow the rules.</i>

284
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:22,106
DON'T BE LATE. NO DRUGS. NO THEFT.

285
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,816
<i>Above all, you may be expelled</i>

286
00:16:23,899 --> 00:16:27,444
<i>if you act in a violent way toward someone</i>
<i>and hurt them.</i>

287
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:28,988
NO EARLY CONFESSION. NO SEXUAL ACTS.

288
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:30,656
Did they make you take a drug test?

289
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,324
- [Ma-kun] I took one.
- Me too.

290
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:35,160
- What kind of dating show does that?
- [all laughing]

291
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,663
- [Hikaru] This one does.
- [Ma-kun] You're gonna get expelled.

292
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:38,580
I know I will.

293
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:39,540
- For real.
- I know it.

294
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:42,251
I feel like I can get along
with everyone for once.

295
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,920
And with that, <i>Badly in Love 2</i> has begun.

296
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:45,838
NAGANO

297
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,214
- Glad to be with you.
- Thank you.

298
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:48,841
- Awich is here.
- [Nagano] Welcome.

299
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:50,843
- We'll be counting on you this time.
- Thank you.

300
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:53,637
[Megumi] I feel like
hip-hop people tend to be more aggressive.

301
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:55,973
And you're in a good place
to understand that.

302
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:58,392
Like, this guy
was about to release a song,

303
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:00,185
- but he got arrested.
- [Nagano exclaims]

304
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:01,937
So the man I married,

305
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:05,024
he was in prison for eight years.

306
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:08,360
- [exclaims]
- Even after he got out, he was in and out.

307
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:09,862
Our house was shot at.

308
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:11,572
- [Megumi] What?
- Huh?

309
00:17:11,655 --> 00:17:13,574
- Your house?
- Like, "Bang, bang, bang."

310
00:17:13,657 --> 00:17:16,326
- So I had to crawl on the floor…
- [Nagano] Oh.

311
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,454
- …just to get around my house.
- [Nagano] Oh, my.

312
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:20,956
- My daughter was a baby at the time.
- Oh.

313
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,458
She was sleeping in her bed,

314
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:25,502
so I had to drag her out of bed
and wait for it to stop.

315
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:28,547
- Seriously?
- Hold on, you're gonna upstage these kids.

316
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:30,424
Like, these participants' lives
are nothing

317
00:17:30,507 --> 00:17:32,009
compared to what you've been though.

318
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:32,968
I'm so sorry.

319
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:36,138
So this time around,
these five men and four women

320
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:38,265
will be living together for two weeks.

321
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:41,435
At the end, they'll confess their feelings
at the graduation ceremony.

322
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:42,352
[bell chiming]

323
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:46,023
[boy on PA] <i>Your first group activity</i>
<i>is making dinner in the kitchen.</i>

324
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:47,566
All right!

325
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:49,610
- [Nagano] <i>Ari is nice.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>They're excited.</i>

326
00:17:49,693 --> 00:17:50,527
LOVE DINER

327
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:51,737
- [Ruru] Cute.
- [Ari] Wow!

328
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,447
- [Assun] You're so loud.
- Wow!

329
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,324
- Wait! It's so cute!
- Oh, wow!

330
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:56,992
- Wow, this is crazy!
- This is amazing!

331
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,578
- A signature Okinawa A&W!
- What is this? It's amazing!

332
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:01,872
- [Hikaru] Super cute.
- [Ari] Burger King or something!

333
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:04,166
[Ruru] No, it's an A&W!

334
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:05,876
- [Leo] Wow.
- [Ruru] This is next level.

335
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:06,794
LOVE DINER

336
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,045
So freakin' cute, you guys!

337
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,130
- This is yankii approved.
- [Maririn] Right.

338
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:13,008
- [Leo] Super stylish.
- There are ingredients for curry.

339
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:15,302
I volunteer to cut the vegetables!

340
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:17,721
- Huh? Bo, you can't cook rice, can you?
- Sure, I can.

341
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,098
[Ruru] Then cook the rice, Bo.

342
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:20,724
What can you do?

343
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:22,518
- Um, vegetables.
- You can cut them?

344
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:24,103
- We'll cut together.
- Let's cut them.

345
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,814
- Want yellow or red?
- I want purple.

346
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:28,232
You want purple?

347
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:30,317
I've been told
purple is a color for horny people.

348
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,861
- Isn't it cute? I like purple the best.
- It is cute, for sure.

349
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,404
- She didn't deny it.
- What'd you say?

350
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:35,781
- Didn't deny she's horny.
- What?

351
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:36,698
Never mind.

352
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,534
Wow, they open up so fast!

353
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:40,327
- They really do.
- [Megumi] Indeed.

354
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,746
- This isn't the fourth day, right?
- No, it's not.

355
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:47,167
- So, you're a model and…
- Right. I'm just a model.

356
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:48,460
- Just a model?
- Yeah.

357
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:50,629
- Nuts Agency?
- Oh, yeah! I'm with them.

358
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,923
- What is it?
- Oh, I just think you're cute.

359
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:54,842
Really? I like that.

360
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:56,844
Lady Ruru.

361
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:58,637
TAI-CHAN (22)
HAIRSTYLIST

362
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:01,348
Lady Ruru really… blew me away.

363
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:03,600
- [Nagano] <i>In love already?</i>
- Her face is too beautiful.

364
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:05,435
It's so cute and small.

365
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:08,480
When she asked me
to do vegetables together,

366
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:10,566
I felt like in that moment, I won.

367
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:11,942
[Nagamo] <i>This kid moves fast.</i>

368
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,694
This is definitely better.

369
00:19:13,777 --> 00:19:16,321
LEO (25)
BAR OWNER

370
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,450
Wow, those are some fancy knife skills.

371
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,119
- Don't make fun of me.
- [laughs]

372
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:25,372
- You seem like a man who can use a knife.
- [chuckles] I'm trying my best.

373
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:26,373
Amazing.

374
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:29,918
It's crazy, you give off
such Kansai-person vibes.

375
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,587
- Me?
- It's a good thing.

376
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:35,424
- I like the Kansai dialect.
- You do?

377
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:36,383
Yeah, I love it.

378
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:41,180
- They have all kinds of alcohol.
- [Hikaru] I can't drink alcohol.

379
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,931
- Can't drink?
- Even though I'm a hostess.

380
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,766
- Not one drop?
- Nope, I'm allergic.

381
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,603
- So, what do you do at work?
- I have soft drinks.

382
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:50,147
- Oh, so that's how it is. Uh-huh.
- Uh-huh.

383
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,858
Do we simmer this?
Whatever. Let's just have a smoke.

384
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:54,193
- Let's do that.
- Let's go.

385
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:55,819
Impromptu smoke break.

386
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:59,364
Know that this dating show
will have a lot of smoking scenes.

387
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:02,659
- [Ruru] Let's go have a smoke.
- Okay, keep cooking. I'll be right back.

388
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:05,287
[Ruru] Where's the smoking area?

389
00:20:07,497 --> 00:20:10,584
- [Leo] You're older than me?
- [Ruru] I'm 26.

390
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:13,295
- Do you like younger girls?
- No, I've only dated older girls.

391
00:20:13,378 --> 00:20:14,296
[Ruru] Oh, really?

392
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,464
Here is fine.

393
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:18,217
- [Awich] <i>Oh, so Ruru is older.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>That's right.</i>

394
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:23,430
- [Ruru] How many girlfriends have you had?
- [Leo] About five or six.

395
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:25,599
Ah. You dumped them, right?

396
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:28,393
Honestly, no.
You'd think so, but I get dumped.

397
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:31,146
- Why? You're a cheater?
- No, I don't cheat.

398
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,564
What'd you do then?

399
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:34,650
My relationship to my friends comes first.

400
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:35,609
Oh, I see.

401
00:20:35,692 --> 00:20:38,362
Often, I had to drop everything
and go somewhere for them.

402
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:42,324
Oh, I really like that.
I like guys who value their friends.

403
00:20:42,407 --> 00:20:45,911
I like them better than other guys
who only focus on their girlfriends.

404
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:48,789
It's more fun that way.
Like, you can take her along with you.

405
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:50,249
- Absolutely.
- Like, for dinner.

406
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,167
If anything, I would want to meet them.

407
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,961
- Right.
- To hang out with them.

408
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:58,090
- Ruru has so much energy, doesn't she?
- Well, she did say she cheats.

409
00:20:58,173 --> 00:21:00,008
- [Nagano] That's true!
- She must be confident.

410
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:00,926
[Megumi] Right.

411
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,971
- [Ruru] How's the food?
- [Ma-kun] It's done.

412
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:06,014
- [Leo] It's tasting great.
- [Ruru] Then let's eat!

413
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:07,391
Let's serve the rice too.

414
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:08,725
- [bell chiming]
- Huh?

415
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:10,811
[Ruru] There's an announcement.

416
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:17,359
[boy on PA]
<i>To all of you who like alcohol…</i>

417
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:18,860
- [Ruru] Yay!
- I love it!

418
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,779
[Maririn] I like it. That's me.

419
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:25,242
<i>…whether you get to drink alcohol today</i>
<i>is up to all of you.</i>

420
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:27,327
- [Ruru] What does that mean?
- [Leo] That's crazy!

421
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:31,581
[boy on PA] <i>If you can cooperate</i>
<i>and complete the task assigned to you,</i>

422
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:34,209
<i>you can have alcohol with dinner.</i>

423
00:21:34,918 --> 00:21:36,044
<i>If you fail…</i>

424
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:38,505
- [Ruru] Huh? No way!
<i>- …there will be no alcohol.</i>

425
00:21:38,588 --> 00:21:41,300
- [Leo] Seriously?
- [Ruru] I definitely want to drink!

426
00:21:41,383 --> 00:21:44,094
Alcohol is
the one important thing in life.

427
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:46,513
- [laughs] My goodness.
- [Awich] So cool.

428
00:21:47,222 --> 00:21:48,682
I might like her.

429
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:50,434
ASSUN (30)
ENTREPRENEUR/HOSTESS

430
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:52,602
I wonder how much I drink in a day.

431
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:55,897
Well, if we're talking about whiskey,
I drink a whole bottle.

432
00:21:56,982 --> 00:22:00,319
[boy on PA]
<i>Everyone, please move to the gym.</i>

433
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:03,405
- [Leo] Let's go.
- What are we gonna do?

434
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:06,491
- It's just a regular gym.
- [Assun] What's the task?

435
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:08,285
- [Maririn] For real?
- [Assun] A jump rope.

436
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:10,120
- [Ruru] It's girly!
- [Maririn] It sparkles!

437
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:11,747
[Ari] Are those spikes? Let's see it.

438
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:15,459
[boy on PA] <i>Your task</i>
<i>is to jump rope 30 times in a row.</i>

439
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:17,836
<i>You only have one chance.</i>

440
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:19,629
- [Ruru] What?
- [Tai-chan] Whoa, 30 times.

441
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:21,882
- [Ruru] Thirty?
- [Leo] Thirty times in a row? Jeez.

442
00:22:21,965 --> 00:22:22,924
[Ma-kun] That's crazy.

443
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:26,136
- Here we go. Ready, set…
- [Maririn] Ready, set…

444
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:29,806
[all] 1, 2, 3, 4…

445
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:32,059
[Nagano] <i>You'd never think</i>
<i>they were fighting earlier.</i>

446
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:34,519
- …7, 8, 9…
- [Megumi] <i>They're cute, aren't they?</i>

447
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:38,106
- [Nagano] <i>They are.</i>
- …10, 11, 12, 13…

448
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:40,275
- [Hikaru shrieks]
- [Megumi] Oh, geez.

449
00:22:40,358 --> 00:22:41,485
No. I wanted to drink.

450
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:44,905
- [Ruru] Please! Give us another chance!
- [Hikaru] Who was it? Who tripped?

451
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:47,407
This happened
because they didn't practice.

452
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:49,326
- They could have practiced.
- [Megumi] Right?

453
00:22:49,409 --> 00:22:51,453
They went at it without even warming up.

454
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:55,415
Please give us another chance!
We only need one more!

455
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:57,709
- We promise!
- [boy on PA] <i>No drinks for you today.</i>

456
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,711
- I'm dead.
- Me too.

457
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:02,756
- [Ruru] One more chance!
- [Leo] No second chances?

458
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:04,466
It was going so well!

459
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:07,511
I think if we just set our minds to it,
we can get it done.

460
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:10,180
- Yeah.
- We've got to make them let us try again.

461
00:23:10,263 --> 00:23:12,516
- [laughs]
- [Awich] <i>They're not giving up.</i>

462
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:14,309
If we get down on our knees and apologize…

463
00:23:14,392 --> 00:23:16,186
- We're yankii.
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.

464
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:18,480
- Don't underestimate us. We can do it.
- Yeah.

465
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:20,440
- That's right.
- Wait, you're doing it?

466
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:22,442
- We're begging you.
- We're sorry.

467
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:25,112
- [Nagano] <i>Why are they looking at us?</i>
- Give us another chance!

468
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:26,613
- Please!
- [Nagano] <i>This feels wrong.</i>

469
00:23:26,696 --> 00:23:27,948
[all] Please!

470
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:29,699
- [Ma-kun] Please!
- [Leo] We'll be good.

471
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:31,034
[Ma-kun] We'll really be good.

472
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:34,538
I've never bowed down on my knees
in my whole life.

473
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:39,960
I'm surprised at what I'm capable of
if alcohol's on the line. [laughs]

474
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:41,294
We'll be good, for real.

475
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:44,381
- [boy on PA] <i>All right, one more chance.</i>
- [all cheering]

476
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:47,050
- [Nagano] <i>Seriously?</i>
- [Megumi] <i>It's their first day.</i>

477
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:49,052
- [Assun] We did it!
- [Ruru] Let's do our best!

478
00:23:49,136 --> 00:23:51,596
- [Maririn] All right.
- Wait, let's huddle up.

479
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,640
- All right. Last one.
- This is our last chance.

480
00:23:53,723 --> 00:23:56,601
- This is our final chance.
- [Ruru] Our final chance. Let's huddle up.

481
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,854
- [Ari] Bring it in.
- Let's jump this rope!

482
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,230
- Come on!
- [all] Let's go!

483
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:02,190
We can do it, we can do it, we can do it!

484
00:24:02,816 --> 00:24:04,651
- Let's do our best. Thirty times.
- Let's go!

485
00:24:04,734 --> 00:24:06,361
- [Hikaru] Here we go.
- [Ari] We got this.

486
00:24:06,444 --> 00:24:08,280
- Thirty times, right?
- Here we go.

487
00:24:08,363 --> 00:24:10,073
- [Ari] Be strong!
- [Bo] All right.

488
00:24:10,157 --> 00:24:11,616
Here we go. Ready, set…

489
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:15,287
[Maririn and Ruru] 1, 2, 3, 4,

490
00:24:15,871 --> 00:24:19,040
5, 6, 7, 8,

491
00:24:19,624 --> 00:24:22,752
9, 10, 11, 12,

492
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:26,798
13, 14, 15, 16,

493
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:31,720
17, 18, 19, 20, 21…

494
00:24:31,803 --> 00:24:34,723
- [Awich] <i>They're gonna do it.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>They just might. Here it comes!</i>

495
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:38,143
…25, 26, 27, 28,

496
00:24:38,226 --> 00:24:39,811
29, 30!

497
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:41,646
- We did it!
- [all cheering]

498
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:44,482
- [Nagano chuckles] <i>No, what is this?</i>
- [Ruru] We did it!

499
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:46,484
[Nagano]
<i>What is this sense of accomplishment?</i>

500
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:49,196
<i>- We have a whole season of episodes first.</i>
- [Assun] We did it!

501
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,616
We are totally badass.

502
00:24:52,699 --> 00:24:55,076
- [panting] That was crazy.
- [Ma-kun] That was insane.

503
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,413
[Ruru] I feel like we're closer now
because of that. What a moment.

504
00:24:58,496 --> 00:25:00,290
- [Ma-kun] I'm glad we did it.
- [Ruru] Right?

505
00:25:00,373 --> 00:25:02,918
I didn't do that stuff
when I was a student.

506
00:25:03,001 --> 00:25:04,419
So I'm living my youth now.

507
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,840
The last time I jumped rope
was a year and a half ago

508
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:10,133
at a sports festival…

509
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:11,927
in prison.

510
00:25:12,010 --> 00:25:15,096
Bo says he hasn't jumped rope
since the prison sports festival.

511
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,098
- He's been in and out.
- [Nagano] No way.

512
00:25:17,182 --> 00:25:18,892
- [boy] <i>Time for dinner.</i>
- [Ari] Let's drink.

513
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:21,645
<i>The alcohol is in the living room.</i>

514
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:24,898
This is so sick. Oh, my God.

515
00:25:24,981 --> 00:25:27,108
- Oh, look at this!
- [Ruru] Oh, so cute!

516
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:29,027
- This is amazing!
- Incredible.

517
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:30,862
[Ari] I can't believe my eyes right now.

518
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:32,447
- This is wild.
- Wow!

519
00:25:32,530 --> 00:25:34,616
- [Ari] Super cool.
- [Ruru] It's too cute!

520
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:37,535
[Maririn] I don't know how to read that.
"This life is all I need"?

521
00:25:37,619 --> 00:25:39,162
- [Ari] The bonsai's huge!
- [Ruru] Cute!

522
00:25:39,246 --> 00:25:40,789
- [Tai-chan] Amazing.
- [Ari] So cool!

523
00:25:40,872 --> 00:25:43,625
- [Assun] I love it.
- [Ari] The art is amazing too.

524
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:45,585
[Ruru] This is the best.

525
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:47,587
- [Leo] I could get used to this.
- [Assun] Sick!

526
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:50,465
- Cheers!
- [all] Cheers!

527
00:25:50,548 --> 00:25:52,425
- [Ari] Wassup?
- [Assun] Yeah.

528
00:25:54,636 --> 00:25:56,471
- Let's eat.
- [Ma-kun] Thanks for the food!

529
00:25:56,554 --> 00:25:58,890
- [Assun] Thank you for the food.
- Whoa, this is so good!

530
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:00,267
[Leo and Maririn] Delicious!

531
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:03,186
[Ari laughs] You're eating too fast.

532
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:04,980
Wait, Tai-chan is so cute.

533
00:26:05,063 --> 00:26:07,941
- [Maririn] He's eating so much.
- [Leo] Don't you just want to feed him?

534
00:26:08,024 --> 00:26:10,777
- [Ma-kun laughs] Right? So cute.
- [Leo] Look at him.

535
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:13,571
It's crazy, it's like maternal instinct.

536
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:16,283
You know, I think Bo is
the most mysterious guy here.

537
00:26:16,366 --> 00:26:18,618
- [Hikaru] I can't read him.
- [Ruru] He doesn't talk much.

538
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:21,329
I really want to know
what has happened to him in his life.

539
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,581
At the end of my first year
of junior high,

540
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:26,876
I was sent to a juvenile assessment center
for beating up a friend.

541
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,378
[Leo exclaims]

542
00:26:28,461 --> 00:26:30,964
Then, a year later,
I was sent to a juvenile training school.

543
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,758
Oh, so you were in there
for quite a long time.

544
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:36,636
- [Bo] Yeah, a long time.
- So you were barely out in the real world?

545
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:38,972
- [Leo] Barely out in your teens.
- [Ruru] Yeah.

546
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:40,890
- What about you, Ma-kun?
- Me?

547
00:26:40,974 --> 00:26:42,892
[Ruru] You're another one
I can't read, Ma-kun.

548
00:26:42,976 --> 00:26:46,980
- [Leo] He's the hardest for me to read.
- I'm pretty normal. I was in a bike gang.

549
00:26:47,063 --> 00:26:50,734
Then became a normal thug,
a normal yakuza, then I quit normally.

550
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:52,944
- [Assun] All normal.
- [Ruru] What about your pinky?

551
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,112
I don't have it anymore.

552
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:55,989
- Seriously?
- [Maririn] You don't?

553
00:26:56,072 --> 00:26:56,990
[Ma-kun] I don't.

554
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:59,909
- [Ruru] Oh, my God. I didn't notice.
- [Ma-kun] I don't.

555
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:03,246
So, yeah,
I just kept going down that path.

556
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:04,873
And then…

557
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:07,375
I had a kid.

558
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:09,711
And after I had a kid, I got arrested.

559
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:13,882
The time you spend with your kid,
when they're still small,

560
00:27:13,965 --> 00:27:15,717
you only have that moment.

561
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:19,220
That made me think,
"This isn't right. I'm so lame."

562
00:27:19,304 --> 00:27:21,806
So I said,
"I'm out. I'd rather be with my kid."

563
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:24,642
And then I started martial arts.

564
00:27:25,643 --> 00:27:26,644
So yeah.

565
00:27:26,728 --> 00:27:28,480
Wow, you are so manly.

566
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:29,773
You're almost too manly.

567
00:27:29,856 --> 00:27:32,817
[Leo] You have a good personality.
That's why people are interested in you.

568
00:27:32,901 --> 00:27:34,194
[Ruru] That's true.

569
00:27:34,277 --> 00:27:36,237
Man, that story really hit me hard.

570
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:38,281
- [laughs]
- [Ruru] You're so cool.

571
00:27:38,365 --> 00:27:40,283
- [Awich] <i>The girls seem into him.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Mmm.</i>

572
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:44,621
I had a kid, and then, I went straight.

573
00:27:46,247 --> 00:27:49,125
I started living a life
where I could go home.

574
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:51,586
But then, somehow,
things started going wrong.

575
00:27:51,669 --> 00:27:55,048
So we decided to start over,
and we broke up.

576
00:27:55,131 --> 00:27:58,593
And then, about six months and a bit ago,

577
00:27:59,219 --> 00:28:00,512
she got remarried.

578
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:03,306
At that time, I also felt…

579
00:28:04,182 --> 00:28:06,393
not so much refreshed, more like…

580
00:28:07,310 --> 00:28:09,396
"Wow, I can finally move on."

581
00:28:09,479 --> 00:28:10,814
And so, I came here.

582
00:28:13,608 --> 00:28:15,902
My family situation was bad too.

583
00:28:15,985 --> 00:28:17,028
I was always out

584
00:28:17,112 --> 00:28:19,239
because I really didn't want
to be at home.

585
00:28:19,906 --> 00:28:22,033
Like, since I was a kid,

586
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:26,663
my mom's boyfriend
would be pretty abusive.

587
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:31,668
When I was 3 or 4, I saw him
punch my mom right in front of me.

588
00:28:31,751 --> 00:28:34,337
Like, he broke her skull and stuff.

589
00:28:35,171 --> 00:28:39,592
She was really beaten up to a pulp.
And I was also beaten up sometimes.

590
00:28:39,676 --> 00:28:41,970
- I want to kill this guy.
- [Ruru laughs]

591
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:44,347
For real, I had welts all over my body.

592
00:28:44,431 --> 00:28:46,015
- Is he still alive?
- [Ruru] He's alive.

593
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:47,142
Then I'll kill him.

594
00:28:47,934 --> 00:28:52,272
Like, yeah, it's true,
I had a pretty tough past. [laughs]

595
00:28:52,355 --> 00:28:54,482
- [Assun] You don't have to laugh.
- Yeah, oh, yeah.

596
00:28:54,566 --> 00:28:55,650
[Ma-kun] Not funny at all.

597
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:58,069
I really want to give you a hug right now.

598
00:28:58,153 --> 00:29:00,488
- [Ruru laughing]
- [Megumi] <i>Look, she's so sweet.</i>

599
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:02,615
[Assun] I feel like crying.

600
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,951
[Leo] I think these girls
are "badly in love."

601
00:29:05,034 --> 00:29:07,036
[laughter]

602
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:09,956
- [Ruru] Thank you, Assun.
- Are you okay? Really? Are you okay?

603
00:29:10,039 --> 00:29:12,959
- I'm okay. I'm living strong now.
- You're strong. That's good.

604
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:15,628
- [Ruru] I'm alive and well.
- [Assun] I feel like crying so much.

605
00:29:16,337 --> 00:29:19,758
- [Ruru] Wait, I want to hear your story.
- I think we're really alike.

606
00:29:19,841 --> 00:29:21,342
- Oh, yeah?
- We're very similar.

607
00:29:21,426 --> 00:29:22,844
We belong to the same group.

608
00:29:22,927 --> 00:29:26,973
Like, my real dad,
I really don't know him,

609
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:29,851
but he was an abuser and a drug dealer.

610
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:33,021
And worse, because he was a drug dealer,

611
00:29:34,314 --> 00:29:37,108
I went through many sad experiences.

612
00:29:37,192 --> 00:29:39,611
So, I really crave company.

613
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:43,656
LIVE IN THE MOMENT

614
00:29:43,740 --> 00:29:46,034
[Ari] That's deep. [inhales deeply]

615
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:50,288
- Hikaru, you're too deep.
- I'm too deep, right?

616
00:29:50,955 --> 00:29:51,998
I'm just sorry…

617
00:29:53,124 --> 00:29:54,584
I can't do anything about it.

618
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,712
- You can listen to me.
- Yeah. [laughs]

619
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:59,297
[Hikaru] I'm counting on you.

620
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:05,220
My ex-girlfriend, I can't forget her.

621
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:06,346
Yeah.

622
00:30:06,429 --> 00:30:07,305
Like…

623
00:30:08,264 --> 00:30:12,310
She keeps popping up
all the time in my mind.

624
00:30:12,393 --> 00:30:15,104
So I can't move on to my next love.

625
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,856
I feel like my ex-girlfriend

626
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:20,151
cast a spell on me
so I can't fall in love with anyone else.

627
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:25,865
I have this old wallet
that I keep in my pocket.

628
00:30:26,699 --> 00:30:30,370
My ex-girlfriend said,
"You can use this. I'll lend it to you."

629
00:30:30,453 --> 00:30:31,788
So I borrowed it.

630
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:34,833
- And we broke up while I had it.
- [Megumi] <i>He's completely worn it out.</i>

631
00:30:34,916 --> 00:30:38,461
I know I shouldn't use it.
Maybe that's why I can't forget her.

632
00:30:39,045 --> 00:30:40,797
At some point soon, though,

633
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:44,676
I'd really like to escape from this
and move on to the next stage.

634
00:30:44,759 --> 00:30:47,095
[Megumi] <i>It sounds like</i>
<i>he's still hung up on her.</i>

635
00:30:47,178 --> 00:30:48,596
SMOKERS' LOUNGE

636
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,681
[Ruru] Bo?

637
00:30:50,473 --> 00:30:52,350
- Huh? Where's Bo?
- [Bo] What's up?

638
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:54,978
Oh, God, I got drunk.

639
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:57,730
Will you listen to my story?

640
00:30:59,148 --> 00:31:00,108
[Ruru] Bo.

641
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:02,277
- [Bo] You cold?
- [Ruru] Huh?

642
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:05,321
[Ma-kun] So kind.

643
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:06,781
A gentleman.

644
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:10,118
[Bo] So, you know,
my friend died last September.

645
00:31:10,201 --> 00:31:11,870
- [Ma-kun] Mmm-hmm.
- My childhood friend.

646
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,037
[Ma-kun] Right.

647
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:15,957
Wait, hold on, tell me properly.

648
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:19,085
- You went to the same junior high, right?
- Same kindergarten.

649
00:31:20,795 --> 00:31:24,132
Going into middle school,
we always had each other's backs.

650
00:31:24,215 --> 00:31:25,049
Mmm.

651
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:26,968
And…

652
00:31:28,469 --> 00:31:31,222
I got a call from a police officer
saying he was missing.

653
00:31:33,349 --> 00:31:35,351
- I thought, "No way."
- Mmm.

654
00:31:37,312 --> 00:31:38,271
And…

655
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:43,151
Well, I heard he was missing,
and I vaguely had a hunch.

656
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:44,068
[Ruru] Mmm.

657
00:31:44,986 --> 00:31:47,906
And, you know,
my house was a hangout spot at the time.

658
00:31:49,157 --> 00:31:51,618
So I went with my <i>aniki</i>
and my brothers to look for him.

659
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:52,535
[Ruru] Mmm.

660
00:31:53,036 --> 00:31:53,870
But I…

661
00:31:54,704 --> 00:31:57,457
I was scared.
I was scared to be the one to find him.

662
00:31:57,540 --> 00:31:58,374
[Ruru] Mmm.

663
00:31:58,458 --> 00:31:59,542
[Bo] So it happened.

664
00:32:00,835 --> 00:32:03,922
And my route to work, well…

665
00:32:04,964 --> 00:32:06,382
passes where my friend died.

666
00:32:10,261 --> 00:32:11,763
Does that mean you saw him?

667
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:19,145
- [crying]
- [Ruru chuckles]

668
00:32:21,856 --> 00:32:24,192
It's okay. That must have been hard.

669
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:25,944
That's painful.

670
00:32:29,030 --> 00:32:31,783
[sniffles] If I'd only
realized it back then…

671
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:37,246
- [sniffles] So I still think about it.
- Mmm.

672
00:32:38,039 --> 00:32:38,957
[sighs]

673
00:32:40,166 --> 00:32:42,710
[sighs] It was the first time
I saw someone die.

674
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:43,962
[Ruru] I see.

675
00:32:45,713 --> 00:32:48,424
If he knew I would be on this show,
he would have been so happy.

676
00:32:48,508 --> 00:32:50,760
[Ruru] Oh, yes.
I'm sure he would have been.

677
00:32:54,013 --> 00:32:57,225
I get it. I don't have
a childhood friend like that, but…

678
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:02,605
but I lost my aunt who I loved so much.

679
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:03,690
So I get it.

680
00:33:05,566 --> 00:33:07,318
But you still have so many regrets, right?

681
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,903
- I do.
- You do?

682
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:11,948
I mean, like,

683
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:16,119
my mom and my home environment
weren't great, right?

684
00:33:16,202 --> 00:33:18,955
So my mom's younger sister, my aunt,

685
00:33:19,706 --> 00:33:24,919
because my home environment was so bad,
she would always move to a place nearby

686
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:28,464
so when things weren't good,
I could run away to her.

687
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:31,718
So I always had a safe place
that wasn't home.

688
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:35,596
- A place like that is important.
- Right.

689
00:33:37,181 --> 00:33:38,558
And, yeah, with my aunt,

690
00:33:39,434 --> 00:33:42,186
she had to go on dialysis and got sick.

691
00:33:43,354 --> 00:33:44,605
And she passed away.

692
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:48,818
- Wanna sit?
- [both laugh]

693
00:33:50,653 --> 00:33:52,405
Yeah, she passed away, but…

694
00:33:53,698 --> 00:33:55,450
[voice breaking] I think about her a lot.

695
00:33:57,493 --> 00:34:01,706
I think if I had taken her to the hospital
sooner, even if it was forcefully,

696
00:34:01,789 --> 00:34:03,833
maybe she wouldn't have passed away.

697
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:05,960
- You're good.
- [chuckles softly]

698
00:34:07,336 --> 00:34:09,672
- So yeah. [sniffles]
- You're a good girl.

699
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:11,924
I think about her a lot.

700
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:15,845
I really liked her so much. [sniffles]

701
00:34:16,429 --> 00:34:18,556
That feeling of losing
someone you cherish,

702
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:20,266
I understand how much it hurts.

703
00:34:20,349 --> 00:34:22,977
- Right? Human life is so fleeting.
- So fleeting. So fleeting.

704
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:25,855
Right? Seriously.
When someone passes, it's so fleeting.

705
00:34:25,938 --> 00:34:29,150
- I wish I could have told her more things.
- Even saying goodbye is fleeting.

706
00:34:29,233 --> 00:34:30,985
Right? It's all so fragile.

707
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:33,988
Seriously, the moment they go
into the fire, it's just so fleeting.

708
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:35,031
[sniffles]

709
00:34:35,823 --> 00:34:38,451
- Like, death is so painful, right?
- Yeah, yeah.

710
00:34:39,869 --> 00:34:43,247
But there are a lot of things
I learned from that experience.

711
00:34:43,331 --> 00:34:45,875
Wow. Bo, you're the best. [laughs]

712
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:50,671
I'm sorry,
but this is the first episode, right?

713
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:51,881
[Megumi] Yes.

714
00:34:51,964 --> 00:34:54,008
This is all happening on the first day.

715
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:55,760
Why did he suddenly open up like that?

716
00:34:55,843 --> 00:34:57,845
- Right? Maybe…
- [Nagano] Maybe what?

717
00:34:57,929 --> 00:35:01,599
Maybe all of them have been
living in such a harsh world.

718
00:35:01,682 --> 00:35:02,517
- Okay.
- [Megumi] Mmm.

719
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:05,228
A world that doesn't follow the rules, so…

720
00:35:05,311 --> 00:35:09,565
the men and women who live in that world,
they never know what's going to happen.

721
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:10,650
[Megumi and Nagano] Mmm.

722
00:35:10,733 --> 00:35:14,654
Living there takes courage,
but they're also taking a lot of risks.

723
00:35:14,737 --> 00:35:17,532
So they might suddenly not be able to
see each other anymore.

724
00:35:17,615 --> 00:35:19,033
- I see.
- [Megumi] That can happen.

725
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:23,121
So you can see why they feel
their world is so fleeting.

726
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:26,666
When they connect
with people who understand that,

727
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:28,709
it just naturally comes out of them.

728
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,753
- [Nagano] It comes out suddenly.
- Their emotions.

729
00:35:30,837 --> 00:35:33,089
I feel like
the show will end after two episodes.

730
00:35:33,172 --> 00:35:34,465
- [laughs]
- I mean, seriously.

731
00:35:34,549 --> 00:35:35,383
[bell chiming]

732
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:38,094
[boy on PA]
<i>The bedrooms are separated by gender.</i>

733
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:40,847
[Hikaru] Oh, no way!

734
00:35:40,930 --> 00:35:44,058
- [Ruru] Wait, this is so cute.
- This is sick! Oh, my God, so great.

735
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:45,560
- This is amazing.
- Wow!

736
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:47,311
- It's so cute!
- This is the best!

737
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:50,439
- For real?
- [Hikaru] It's so cute.

738
00:35:50,523 --> 00:35:53,442
- [Assun] I'm so hyped, girls, so hyped.
- [Hikaru] So sick.

739
00:35:53,526 --> 00:35:57,280
[Ruru] Hey, wait, it's so yellow.
A happy yellow!

740
00:35:57,363 --> 00:36:00,449
- [Maririn] Oh, wow, it's so cute.
- [Hikaru] It's so cute!

741
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:04,412
Hey, look, see that? "Madly in love."

742
00:36:04,495 --> 00:36:07,582
- [Hikaru and Ruru] "Madly in love."
- [Hikaru] We have arrived!

743
00:36:08,082 --> 00:36:11,252
- [Leo] We're over here?
- [Ma-kun] I can't wait to see it.

744
00:36:11,335 --> 00:36:13,171
- [Tai-chan] Here I go.
- [Ma-kun] Let's go in.

745
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:14,630
I can already see it's amazing.

746
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:16,174
- This is crazy.
- Oh, my God.

747
00:36:16,924 --> 00:36:19,260
- [Ari] What? How is it?
- It's amazing. So sick.

748
00:36:19,343 --> 00:36:21,095
- Wow, it's so big.
- [Leo] Now we're talking.

749
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:22,597
- [Tai-chan] Amazing.
- [Leo] My God.

750
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:24,640
- [Ma-kun] So sick.
- [Tai-chan] This is massive.

751
00:36:24,724 --> 00:36:27,226
- [Ma-kun] It's so cool.
- [Leo] It's so nice.

752
00:36:27,310 --> 00:36:28,311
[Tai-chan] Incredible.

753
00:36:29,187 --> 00:36:30,021
[Leo] I love it.

754
00:36:30,104 --> 00:36:32,106
[Tai-chan] This is the best. So cool.

755
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:34,984
- It's so nice.
- [Ari] This is so insane.

756
00:36:35,067 --> 00:36:37,403
- [Leo] Hell yeah!
- [Tai-chan] Wow, it's awesome!

757
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:39,071
[Ari] Is this okay?

758
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:40,907
It's scary.

759
00:36:42,158 --> 00:36:43,451
No katanas, bro.

760
00:36:43,534 --> 00:36:44,702
BADASS

761
00:36:44,785 --> 00:36:45,703
BAD BITCH

762
00:36:45,786 --> 00:36:47,872
[Ruru] I don't know about you girls, but…

763
00:36:48,539 --> 00:36:51,542
don't you feel motivated
to open up and fall in love?

764
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:53,878
- [Hikaru] Mmm.
- [Assun] Oh, that's good.

765
00:36:53,961 --> 00:36:56,756
The one I think has strong principles
would be Ma-kun.

766
00:36:56,839 --> 00:36:58,299
Ah.

767
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:01,010
The one I want to get to know more
is Tai-chan.

768
00:37:01,093 --> 00:37:02,011
[Ruru] Oh, really?

769
00:37:02,094 --> 00:37:04,764
And the one that I think

770
00:37:04,847 --> 00:37:07,350
is truest to his principles
is the same one you said.

771
00:37:07,433 --> 00:37:09,310
[Ruru] Yeah, that's true.
That makes sense.

772
00:37:09,393 --> 00:37:11,479
- Everyone would think that.
- [Ruru] That makes sense.

773
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:15,566
I mean, the people I've dated so far
have all been like that.

774
00:37:15,650 --> 00:37:18,277
I mean, I really thought Ma-kun and I
were on the same wavelength.

775
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:19,779
- Mmm.
- [Ruru] That's what I thought.

776
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:21,614
You know who else?

777
00:37:21,697 --> 00:37:24,575
- Leo. I think Leo is fun too.
- [all] Ah.

778
00:37:24,659 --> 00:37:28,079
- And I really like funny guys.
- That Kansai dialect.

779
00:37:28,162 --> 00:37:31,040
- [Assun] Yeah.
- But Ma-kun… is nice.

780
00:37:31,123 --> 00:37:33,417
The four of us
are going to fight over him.

781
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:34,877
- [Ruru] What?
- [Assun] Over Ma-kun.

782
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:37,797
- [Ruru] I'm gonna go all out.
- [laughs] Today? On day one?

783
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,298
[Ruru] I'm gonna go all out,

784
00:37:39,382 --> 00:37:41,676
but Ma-kun seems like
he likes older women.

785
00:37:41,759 --> 00:37:44,595
- [Hikaru whispers] I know.
- [Ruru] But I'm not gonna lose.

786
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:46,681
- I'm not gonna lose.
- [Assun] I'm not gonna lose.

787
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:48,557
- I'm not.
- [Assun] I'm not gonna lose either.

788
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:50,935
Don't try to cover your face.
I'm not gonna lose.

789
00:37:51,018 --> 00:37:52,603
- I'm not gonna lose.
- [Assun laughing]

790
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:54,855
I'm not gonna lose.

791
00:37:55,439 --> 00:37:56,899
[bell chiming]

792
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:59,568
[boy on PA]
<i>Now, each of you will write a love letter</i>

793
00:37:59,652 --> 00:38:02,113
<i>- to the person you're interested in.</i>
- [Ruru] Here it is.

794
00:38:03,281 --> 00:38:04,198
Just one though?

795
00:38:04,782 --> 00:38:07,201
[boy on PA]
<i>Write a love letter anonymously</i>

796
00:38:07,285 --> 00:38:08,953
<i>to the one person you felt something for…</i>

797
00:38:09,036 --> 00:38:09,870
[Assun] Oh?

798
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:12,123
<i>…and put it in their mailbox</i>
<i>when you're done.</i>

799
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:13,207
[Hikaru] Anonymously?

800
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:15,501
- [Nagano] <i>Here we go.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Who're they thinking of?</i>

801
00:38:15,584 --> 00:38:18,337
[sentimental rock music playing]

802
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:20,089
LEO

803
00:38:22,425 --> 00:38:23,843
MA-KUN

804
00:38:23,926 --> 00:38:25,136
YOU'RE THE ONE I'M…

805
00:38:27,054 --> 00:38:28,264
TO TAI-CHAN

806
00:38:35,563 --> 00:38:37,148
ASSUN, YOU'RE STRONG-WILLED

807
00:38:40,484 --> 00:38:42,778
BY INSTINCT, I THOUGHT…

808
00:38:46,449 --> 00:38:48,200
MA-KUN (28)
MMA FIGHTER

809
00:38:49,243 --> 00:38:50,870
[Megumi] <i>Who's getting Ma-kun's letter?</i>

810
00:38:51,412 --> 00:38:53,164
- [Nagano] <i>Oh!</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Oh, it's Assun.</i>

811
00:38:56,959 --> 00:38:58,294
She looks out for people.

812
00:38:59,003 --> 00:39:01,797
That consideration towards others
is something you're born with.

813
00:39:02,381 --> 00:39:05,843
I felt she's someone who thinks like I do.

814
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:06,761
ARI (29)
RAPPER/MODEL

815
00:39:06,844 --> 00:39:08,679
- [exhales deeply]
- [Nagano] <i>What about Ari?</i>

816
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:12,183
[Megumi] <i>He put it in Hikaru's.</i>

817
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:18,981
I haven't met anyone with blonde hair
and a snaggletooth in a while.

818
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:21,192
So I was like, "Wow, she's awesome."

819
00:39:21,901 --> 00:39:24,987
I was like, "Should I confess to her
tomorrow or maybe today?"

820
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:28,282
BO (27)
COMMERCIAL PAINTER

821
00:39:28,866 --> 00:39:30,326
- [Nagano] <i>It's Bo.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Bo.</i>

822
00:39:30,409 --> 00:39:32,411
[Nagano]
<i>Bo's gonna give his letter to that girl.</i>

823
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:34,413
- [Megumi] <i>Ruru.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Right?</i>

824
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:36,999
[Bo] <i>I wrote my letter</i>
<i>to this person called Ruru.</i>

825
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,919
She seemed to value those close to her.

826
00:39:40,544 --> 00:39:42,755
I felt she had a burning passion.

827
00:39:42,838 --> 00:39:44,715
TAI-CHAN (22)
HAIRSTYLIST

828
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:48,386
RURU

829
00:39:50,679 --> 00:39:52,431
Lady Ruru, man, that girl…

830
00:39:53,099 --> 00:39:54,767
She and I need to talk, for real.

831
00:39:55,643 --> 00:39:56,644
LEO (25)
BAR OWNER

832
00:39:56,727 --> 00:39:58,187
[Nagano] <i>What about Leo?</i>

833
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:00,147
[Leo] <i>Been a while</i>
<i>since I wrote a love letter.</i>

834
00:40:00,231 --> 00:40:01,649
[Nagano] <i>Ah, he put it in Ruru's.</i>

835
00:40:01,732 --> 00:40:04,944
Because I like Ruru's face. It's cute.

836
00:40:05,027 --> 00:40:07,363
Ruru's the one I liked the most today.

837
00:40:07,446 --> 00:40:10,449
ASSUN (30)
ENTREPRENEUR/HOSTESS

838
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,618
[Nagano] <i>What about Assun?</i>

839
00:40:15,538 --> 00:40:17,748
- [Megumi] <i>Ma-kun, it's mutual!</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Ah!</i>

840
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:20,668
He has the strongest backbone.

841
00:40:20,751 --> 00:40:22,253
He's so firm.

842
00:40:22,837 --> 00:40:27,633
I think he really has the kind
of personality that I like in a guy.

843
00:40:27,716 --> 00:40:30,719
HIKARU (23)
HOSTESS

844
00:40:32,179 --> 00:40:36,350
MA-KUN

845
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:38,811
He's the first letter in kanji.
He's an alpha.

846
00:40:40,312 --> 00:40:42,314
Like, he's definitely the most popular.

847
00:40:43,357 --> 00:40:45,651
MARIRIN (25)
BAR WORKER

848
00:40:45,734 --> 00:40:48,028
[Nagano]
<i>Maririn, who's she gonna give it to?</i>

849
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:52,741
<i>- Ooh!</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Tai-chan.</i>

850
00:40:53,617 --> 00:40:55,411
Everyone said Ma-kun,

851
00:40:55,494 --> 00:40:59,457
but he looks so much like my ex,
and he was also a thug.

852
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:03,002
My thug ex-boyfriend took all my money.

853
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:06,213
Like, I had a flashback and got scared.

854
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:11,010
That might be why
I felt a bit more interested in Tai-chan.

855
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:12,511
[Nagano] <i>Maririn seems a bit shy.</i>

856
00:41:12,595 --> 00:41:14,263
RURU (26)
MODEL

857
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:16,640
[Megumi] <i>What about Ruru,</i>
<i>the most popular girl?</i>

858
00:41:19,894 --> 00:41:21,103
[Nagano and Megumi] <i>Oh!</i>

859
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:23,189
[Nagano] <i>So that's how it is.</i>

860
00:41:24,190 --> 00:41:26,775
If there's a letter from Leo
in my mailbox,

861
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:29,820
then that's it, I'm going all in on him.

862
00:41:29,904 --> 00:41:32,031
- [Nagano] <i>All in, huh?</i>
- If there isn't, we're done.

863
00:41:32,114 --> 00:41:34,909
Like, fuck you. Just like that.

864
00:41:34,992 --> 00:41:35,826
"Fuck you."

865
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:38,662
She knows what that means in English,
doesn't she?

866
00:41:38,746 --> 00:41:39,788
So, as you can see,

867
00:41:39,872 --> 00:41:42,082
- the romances are starting to take shape.
- [Nagano] Yes.

868
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:45,294
Ma-kun seems to be
very popular among the girls.

869
00:41:45,377 --> 00:41:47,087
- They seem to like him.
- [Megumi] Mmm.

870
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:49,215
I think he's the scariest one
out of all the group.

871
00:41:49,298 --> 00:41:50,216
[Megumi] Huh?

872
00:41:50,299 --> 00:41:52,426
- Why do you say that? He seems nice.
- [Megumi] Right?

873
00:41:52,510 --> 00:41:55,054
If he can keep up that nice attitude,

874
00:41:55,137 --> 00:41:58,224
it means he doesn't have
to put on a tough face.

875
00:41:58,307 --> 00:41:59,141
Ah.

876
00:41:59,225 --> 00:42:02,978
So I think that deep down,
he may be really confident and strong.

877
00:42:03,062 --> 00:42:04,230
- [Nagano] Right.
- [Megumi] Oh.

878
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:07,066
If well-channeled,
that can turn out to be a very good thing.

879
00:42:07,149 --> 00:42:10,444
But if it goes in a bad direction,
I think it can be really scary.

880
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:12,196
- I see.
- [Nagano] Ah!

881
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:15,699
How do you know that? You're amazing.

882
00:42:15,783 --> 00:42:20,829
And then, that same Ma-kun
wrote his letter to Assun, right?

883
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:23,999
- And Assun wrote back to Ma-kun.
- Mmm. Oh.

884
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:26,043
And Hikaru also wrote hers to Ma-kun.

885
00:42:26,126 --> 00:42:28,379
And Ari wrote to Hikaru.

886
00:42:28,462 --> 00:42:30,381
- And Maririn wrote to Tai-chan.
- Right.

887
00:42:30,923 --> 00:42:33,551
Ruru got letters
from Leo, Tai-chan, and Bo.

888
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:37,096
- And Ruru wrote hers to Leo, right?
- [Nagano] Mmm.

889
00:42:37,846 --> 00:42:40,432
So Ma-kun and Ruru
are very popular this time.

890
00:42:40,516 --> 00:42:43,852
Yes, and they seem to have good matches
for themselves, don't they?

891
00:42:43,936 --> 00:42:46,272
- Their interest is mutual.
- Ma-kun, yeah, but for Leo…

892
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:47,606
- I don't know.
- That's right.

893
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:50,693
In any case, Ruru is very confident.

894
00:42:50,776 --> 00:42:51,860
- In herself.
- In herself.

895
00:42:51,944 --> 00:42:52,820
[Megumi] Mmm, mmm.

896
00:42:52,903 --> 00:42:56,907
And I think she wants to see
what other people are like first.

897
00:42:56,991 --> 00:42:58,367
- [Megumi] Ah!
- Oh!

898
00:42:58,951 --> 00:43:01,829
- She's strategizing. Ah.
- I think she has a strategy, for sure.

899
00:43:01,912 --> 00:43:05,541
If that's true,
that would be interesting. I'm curious.

900
00:43:11,755 --> 00:43:13,340
[Nagano] Hey, what's wrong, Bo?

901
00:43:14,758 --> 00:43:15,926
Hey, what happened?

902
00:43:17,094 --> 00:43:18,846
- [Tai-chan] Let's decide.
- [Bo] Two of us?

903
00:43:18,929 --> 00:43:20,055
[Tai-chan] Yes, two of us.

904
00:43:20,139 --> 00:43:21,181
Oh, are you okay?

905
00:43:21,724 --> 00:43:23,976
- So-so. [chuckles]
- [Leo] Are you good?

906
00:43:24,059 --> 00:43:25,185
My contact lenses.

907
00:43:26,020 --> 00:43:29,607
My eye got injured from some liquid,
so I'm going to the hospital.

908
00:43:29,690 --> 00:43:31,650
- What? Wait.
- [Megumi laughs]

909
00:43:31,734 --> 00:43:34,612
- He even says it like a delinquent.
- He may be quite clumsy.

910
00:43:35,571 --> 00:43:36,530
Seriously?

911
00:43:37,114 --> 00:43:38,449
I'll pray for your safety.

912
00:43:38,532 --> 00:43:39,867
- [Bo] Thanks.
- [Leo] Yeah.

913
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:43,329
- I'm getting really nervous.
- [Ma-kun] For real.

914
00:43:43,412 --> 00:43:44,538
- I get that.
- [Leo] Right?

915
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:47,458
If you go first and come back
with a letter, I'll stab you.

916
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:48,834
- Why me?
- I mean it. Yeah.

917
00:43:48,917 --> 00:43:50,628
- [Ari] I'm going to go.
- [Leo] Mmm.

918
00:43:51,462 --> 00:43:54,465
[breathes deeply]

919
00:43:54,548 --> 00:43:55,549
Smell you later.

920
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:58,052
[Leo] He looks so relaxed.

921
00:43:59,553 --> 00:44:02,097
- [Megumi] <i>I wonder if there is one.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>I see.</i>

922
00:44:02,181 --> 00:44:03,682
[Megumi] <i>They'll pick up the letters.</i>

923
00:44:04,767 --> 00:44:06,894
Seriously? I don't wanna open it. [sighs]

924
00:44:06,977 --> 00:44:08,979
[pleasant music playing]

925
00:44:10,564 --> 00:44:11,857
Please let there be one.

926
00:44:15,611 --> 00:44:17,279
- [Megumi] <i>Zero.</i>
- [Awich] <i>Nothing.</i>

927
00:44:25,162 --> 00:44:26,413
[Tai-chan] Oh, he's back.

928
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:31,001
[Ma-kun] He must've gotten one.

929
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:34,755
- [Tai-chan] He got zero.
- Hello there.

930
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:38,425
You seem so confident.
You got one, didn't you?

931
00:44:39,176 --> 00:44:40,094
[sighs]

932
00:44:45,891 --> 00:44:47,226
- [Nagano] <i>Oh!</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Ah!</i>

933
00:44:47,309 --> 00:44:49,061
<i>- He's happy, I'm sure.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Sure he is.</i>

934
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:55,317
[humming]

935
00:45:01,907 --> 00:45:03,534
[Megumi] <i>Oh, Mr. Popular.</i>

936
00:45:06,078 --> 00:45:08,455
- Whoa.
- [Megumi] <i>Ruru put hers in there.</i>

937
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:16,422
LEO, YOUR KANSAI DIALECT
REALLY LIGHTENS THE MOOD!

938
00:45:16,505 --> 00:45:18,757
LET'S HAVE FUN UNTIL THE LAST DAY

939
00:45:22,553 --> 00:45:25,347
My heart is just like
Tom and Jerry right now.

940
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:28,058
<i>It's going like, "Bum, bum, bum, bum."</i>

941
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:32,020
This is more than just a "like."
It's love.

942
00:45:35,149 --> 00:45:36,984
You're grinning so much.

943
00:45:37,568 --> 00:45:39,069
- Congratulations.
- What?

944
00:45:39,153 --> 00:45:40,529
- Am I that obvious?
- [Ari] You are.

945
00:45:40,612 --> 00:45:42,614
- You're obvious, bro. So obvious.
- [Leo] Really?

946
00:45:42,698 --> 00:45:44,158
[Ari] I didn't get any, you know?

947
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:46,034
- [Leo] Huh?
- I didn't get any.

948
00:45:46,118 --> 00:45:48,203
But you got one,
you got another, and I got two.

949
00:45:48,287 --> 00:45:50,622
Oh, did you figure out
who the message was from?

950
00:45:50,706 --> 00:45:52,291
- I don't know.
- [Leo] I think Assun.

951
00:45:52,374 --> 00:45:53,709
- Assun's is in here.
- [Leo] Yeah.

952
00:45:53,792 --> 00:45:56,003
- Who do you think it's from?
- I think mine is from Ruru.

953
00:45:56,587 --> 00:45:58,797
[Ma-kun and Tai-chan] Oh!

954
00:45:58,881 --> 00:46:01,091
- [Leo] Hmm.
- Then who could mine be from?

955
00:46:01,175 --> 00:46:03,135
- The only one left is Hikaru, right?
- Hikaru?

956
00:46:03,218 --> 00:46:04,803
You suddenly become conscious of them.

957
00:46:04,887 --> 00:46:05,888
- Don't you?
- [Leo] Yeah.

958
00:46:05,971 --> 00:46:08,307
- [Tai-chan] You do?
- [Leo] Of who wrote it.

959
00:46:08,390 --> 00:46:10,350
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.
- [Leo] You're conscious of them.

960
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:11,518
I'M MOST INTERESTED IN YOU.

961
00:46:11,602 --> 00:46:13,687
- This is major.
- [Ma-kun] It really is.

962
00:46:13,770 --> 00:46:16,773
- [Leo] A huge step forward.
- [Ma-kun] It really moves your heart.

963
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:19,818
- It's touching.
- [Ari] Makes you feel positive about love.

964
00:46:19,902 --> 00:46:21,487
I WANT TO TALK TO YOU MORE!

965
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:22,779
- [Leo] Yeah.
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.

966
00:46:22,863 --> 00:46:25,032
[Ari] It makes you
look forward to falling in love.

967
00:46:25,115 --> 00:46:26,450
Well, to be honest,

968
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:29,912
I don't know if the girl who wrote
a letter to me is really Hikaru.

969
00:46:30,787 --> 00:46:32,206
But I think it's Hikaru.

970
00:46:34,708 --> 00:46:36,960
But then, I also wrote a letter to Ruru.

971
00:46:37,586 --> 00:46:38,712
So, for me,

972
00:46:40,005 --> 00:46:42,758
I can't think of anyone else
other than those two.

973
00:46:42,841 --> 00:46:44,051
That's where I'm at now.

974
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:47,054
Tai-chan's misunderstanding
is making him think

975
00:46:47,137 --> 00:46:49,264
the love letter he received
was from Hikaru.

976
00:46:49,348 --> 00:46:51,892
Now he thinks she's into him,
he's like, "Hikaru seems nice."

977
00:46:51,975 --> 00:46:55,229
- Oh, so that's what's happening!
- Right. It was Maririn.

978
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:56,813
- That's right.
- He's got it wrong.

979
00:46:56,897 --> 00:46:58,273
- Exactly.
- What a shame.

980
00:46:58,357 --> 00:47:00,067
Yeah, right?

981
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:02,528
Congratulations.

982
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:05,697
Don't say "congratulations."
It's not like we're a couple already.

983
00:47:06,198 --> 00:47:08,033
- You should move on.
- It's just beginning.

984
00:47:08,116 --> 00:47:09,159
- Right?
- There's more time.

985
00:47:09,243 --> 00:47:11,578
It's like going
from a rice bowl to a rice box.

986
00:47:13,830 --> 00:47:14,957
I'm not sure I get that.

987
00:47:15,040 --> 00:47:16,124
- Don't get it?
- [Leo] Nope.

988
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:18,252
Like going from a beef bowl
to a cheese beef bowl.

989
00:47:18,335 --> 00:47:21,004
More like going from conveyor belt sushi
to high-end sushi.

990
00:47:21,088 --> 00:47:22,339
Ooh!

991
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:25,759
- Like sushi in Ginza, huh?
- You're fired as a rapper.

992
00:47:25,842 --> 00:47:27,344
- He's the rapper now.
- [laughs]

993
00:47:27,427 --> 00:47:29,638
What do you mean? It was just an analogy.

994
00:47:31,473 --> 00:47:33,559
[Megumi] <i>Okay, it's the girls' turn.</i>

995
00:47:33,642 --> 00:47:34,726
[excitedly] Ooh!

996
00:47:36,228 --> 00:47:37,521
I don't think I have any.

997
00:47:39,648 --> 00:47:40,566
[gasps]

998
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:43,068
[giggles]

999
00:47:44,861 --> 00:47:46,488
[giggling]

1000
00:47:46,572 --> 00:47:48,824
- [Megumi] <i>And she's running.</i>
- Oh, my goodness.

1001
00:47:48,907 --> 00:47:51,118
- She ran over here.
- [laughing]

1002
00:47:51,201 --> 00:47:52,411
We know what that means.

1003
00:47:53,370 --> 00:47:54,788
- Ta-da!
- [Ruru] Yay!

1004
00:47:54,871 --> 00:47:56,748
- I got a letter!
- [Nagano] <i>She's adorable.</i>

1005
00:47:56,832 --> 00:47:58,542
- [Megumi] <i>So cute.</i>
- That's so nice!

1006
00:47:58,625 --> 00:48:01,461
TO HIKARU: WASSUP! WHEN I FIRST SAW YOU
TODAY, I LOVED YOUR BLONDE HAIR

1007
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:03,797
[Megumi] <i>"Wassup."</i>
<i>She'll figure it out. He made it easy.</i>

1008
00:48:03,880 --> 00:48:06,049
AND YOUR SNAGGLETOOTH IS JUST PERFECT TOO

1009
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:08,677
[Awich] <i>He even mentioned</i>
<i>the blonde hair and the snaggletooth.</i>

1010
00:48:08,760 --> 00:48:11,096
- It's so cute.
- [Assun and Ruru] Oh!

1011
00:48:11,179 --> 00:48:12,806
- [Ruru] You're grinning!
- It's so packed.

1012
00:48:12,889 --> 00:48:14,182
- The whole paper.
- [Ruru] Really?

1013
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:15,100
Yeah.

1014
00:48:15,183 --> 00:48:17,394
All of a sudden,
she has the face of someone in love.

1015
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:21,148
- Okay, this is pretty hot.
- [all laughing]

1016
00:48:21,231 --> 00:48:23,150
I'm in heat. I feel like a woman.

1017
00:48:24,067 --> 00:48:26,069
[pensive rock music playing]

1018
00:48:30,324 --> 00:48:31,408
[Nagano] <i>Oh, Maririn.</i>

1019
00:48:48,717 --> 00:48:50,636
- Well, I'm back.
- [Ruru] Welcome back.

1020
00:48:52,596 --> 00:48:54,264
Who could it be?

1021
00:48:54,348 --> 00:48:56,725
Huh? Shall we do it? Shall we show them?

1022
00:48:56,808 --> 00:48:57,893
This is Leo.

1023
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:01,897
- It's Leo.
- [Megumi] <i>Girls can really tell.</i>

1024
00:49:01,980 --> 00:49:04,149
[Hikaru] "To begin with, I'm not 35."

1025
00:49:04,232 --> 00:49:06,443
- [Ruru] This is from Tai-chan.
- Oh?

1026
00:49:07,361 --> 00:49:09,988
[Hikaru]
"I honestly thought you were cute."

1027
00:49:10,072 --> 00:49:11,531
"I want to talk to you more."

1028
00:49:11,615 --> 00:49:13,533
- [Assun] "You're cute."
- How do you know?

1029
00:49:13,617 --> 00:49:14,951
Because we were in the kitchen.

1030
00:49:15,035 --> 00:49:16,745
- This is Tai-chan.
- He said you're cute.

1031
00:49:16,828 --> 00:49:18,246
[Ruru] I don't know who this is.

1032
00:49:18,330 --> 00:49:20,832
- [Maririn] It's written vertically.
- [Hikaru] Isn't this Bo?

1033
00:49:20,916 --> 00:49:22,417
[Ruru] You also think it's Bo?

1034
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:24,920
- [Maririn] How old is he?
- [Hikaru] "I live by my instincts."

1035
00:49:25,003 --> 00:49:26,838
- [Assun] Sounds like Bo.
- [Ruru] Does it?

1036
00:49:26,922 --> 00:49:29,466
So, Bo wrote it vertically, huh?

1037
00:49:29,549 --> 00:49:30,884
- Like a prisoner.
- [Megumi] Yeah.

1038
00:49:30,967 --> 00:49:32,928
No, prisoners also write horizontally.

1039
00:49:33,011 --> 00:49:34,346
- They do?
- How do you know?

1040
00:49:34,429 --> 00:49:35,305
How do you know?

1041
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:38,600
[chuckling] There are also letters
written horizontally.

1042
00:49:38,684 --> 00:49:40,310
- That's Ma-kun.
- [Hikaru] Mmm-hmm.

1043
00:49:40,394 --> 00:49:41,812
- Really?
- Yeah, it's Ma-kun.

1044
00:49:42,854 --> 00:49:44,856
- [Hikaru] What does it say?
- [Maririn] I wanna see.

1045
00:49:44,940 --> 00:49:47,150
[Assun] "I like how you're a tomboy,

1046
00:49:47,234 --> 00:49:50,278
but you're also considerate of others."

1047
00:49:50,362 --> 00:49:51,738
"I also like how you look."

1048
00:49:51,822 --> 00:49:53,407
- [Ruru] Isn't that Ma-kun?
- [women] Aw!

1049
00:49:54,366 --> 00:49:55,617
Oh, I'm so happy.

1050
00:49:55,701 --> 00:49:57,494
- That's nice, isn't it?
- [Maririn] So sweet.

1051
00:49:57,577 --> 00:50:00,122
Isn't it so awesome
you got the one from Ma-kun?

1052
00:50:00,789 --> 00:50:02,374
So it's mutual for both of you.

1053
00:50:02,958 --> 00:50:04,543
- Huh? This guy?
- [Hikaru] That's right.

1054
00:50:04,626 --> 00:50:05,460
Oh, that's true.

1055
00:50:06,169 --> 00:50:08,088
- We don't know for sure yet.
- Yeah.

1056
00:50:08,672 --> 00:50:11,091
When I opened it,
there were three letters in there.

1057
00:50:11,174 --> 00:50:13,802
So I thought,
"There it is, I'm officially popular."

1058
00:50:13,885 --> 00:50:16,263
I'm on fire. Just like that.

1059
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:18,473
- [Maririn] There they are.
- [Assun] They're here.

1060
00:50:18,557 --> 00:50:20,100
- Good morning.
- Hey, girls.

1061
00:50:20,183 --> 00:50:21,143
[Ari] Hey.

1062
00:50:21,226 --> 00:50:23,687
- I'm not seeing Bo here.
- Is he still not better?

1063
00:50:23,770 --> 00:50:25,772
- Not yet. He's at the hospital.
- [Hikaru] That bad?

1064
00:50:26,481 --> 00:50:27,899
I hope he's okay.

1065
00:50:27,983 --> 00:50:29,818
- He went to the hospital.
- I'm so worried.

1066
00:50:30,402 --> 00:50:32,154
None of you did this to him, right?

1067
00:50:32,237 --> 00:50:33,113
- Hmm?
- To Bo.

1068
00:50:33,822 --> 00:50:35,991
- No way.
- You didn't make his eyes swell up?

1069
00:50:37,075 --> 00:50:38,744
- Oh, he's here.
- [Ruru] He's back.

1070
00:50:38,827 --> 00:50:40,704
- [Ma-kun] There he is.
- I'm back.

1071
00:50:40,787 --> 00:50:43,999
- [Assun] Welcome back.
- [Hikaru] What a cool entrance!

1072
00:50:44,082 --> 00:50:45,542
- [Leo] You got jumped.
- Yeah, right.

1073
00:50:45,625 --> 00:50:47,836
- Leo did this while I slept.
- I what?

1074
00:50:47,919 --> 00:50:49,421
- [Bo laughs]
- I knew it.

1075
00:50:49,504 --> 00:50:51,173
- [Leo] Hey.
- [Ruru] You okay?

1076
00:50:51,256 --> 00:50:53,049
- It was my contacts.
- [Ruru] Aw.

1077
00:50:53,133 --> 00:50:54,926
- [Ari] I'm glad you made it back.
- Yeah.

1078
00:50:55,510 --> 00:50:58,305
Bo, you didn't get any letters.
Don't feel bad.

1079
00:50:58,388 --> 00:51:00,682
- I get it, I get it. [laughs]
- [bell chiming]

1080
00:51:00,766 --> 00:51:02,893
[boy on PA] <i>It's the afternoon sauna time.</i>

1081
00:51:02,976 --> 00:51:03,894
- Huh?
- [Ma-kun] Yeah!

1082
00:51:03,977 --> 00:51:05,979
[boy on PA] <i>The one who can go in is…</i>

1083
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:07,981
[Megumi]
<i>They get closer to each other in there.</i>

1084
00:51:08,064 --> 00:51:10,776
<i>…the one who got the most love letters.</i>

1085
00:51:10,859 --> 00:51:11,985
- Oh, here we go.
<i>- Ruru.</i>

1086
00:51:12,569 --> 00:51:13,487
[Leo] What?

1087
00:51:13,570 --> 00:51:15,489
- [Hikaru] You didn't know?
- [Ma-kun] I didn't.

1088
00:51:15,572 --> 00:51:17,491
[Hikaru]
You don't know who sent letters to who?

1089
00:51:17,574 --> 00:51:19,659
- [Leo] No, I don't.
- No, we do. We do, right?

1090
00:51:19,743 --> 00:51:23,622
[boy on PA] <i>Ruru, please choose</i>
<i>the man you want to go with.</i>

1091
00:51:24,748 --> 00:51:26,374
- [Ma-kun] Right now?
- [all laugh]

1092
00:51:26,458 --> 00:51:28,168
- [Leo] When else?
- [Ma-kun] Here and now?

1093
00:51:28,251 --> 00:51:29,085
[Ruru groans]

1094
00:51:29,169 --> 00:51:30,670
- Then?
- What?

1095
00:51:30,754 --> 00:51:31,963
- [Ruru laughs]
- You know.

1096
00:51:32,047 --> 00:51:33,548
- Shut up.
- [women laughing]

1097
00:51:33,632 --> 00:51:34,674
Look what he did.

1098
00:51:34,758 --> 00:51:36,676
- That was so cute, seriously.
- [Leo] What was?

1099
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:38,470
- [Assun] So cute.
- Don't look at me.

1100
00:51:38,553 --> 00:51:41,223
- You made a cute face, bro.
- [Leo] Stop looking at me.

1101
00:51:41,306 --> 00:51:42,599
You should make it more.

1102
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:45,435
The sauna. Uh…

1103
00:51:47,604 --> 00:51:49,189
- Who wants to go with me?
- Me!

1104
00:51:49,272 --> 00:51:51,191
[women laughing]

1105
00:51:51,274 --> 00:51:52,859
- [Ruru] Just one?
- [Ma-kun] So cute.

1106
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:54,778
- Go with someone who wants it.
- True.

1107
00:51:54,861 --> 00:51:56,446
But since it's the first time,

1108
00:51:56,530 --> 00:51:59,115
I want to go with someone
I can have a deep conversation with.

1109
00:51:59,199 --> 00:52:01,910
- Right, who do you want that to be?
- [Leo] Oh, my God.

1110
00:52:02,494 --> 00:52:03,328
Shut up.

1111
00:52:08,875 --> 00:52:09,751
[Ruru] Mmm…

1112
00:52:11,461 --> 00:52:12,963
Okay, I've decided.

1113
00:52:15,590 --> 00:52:16,424
Let's go.

1114
00:52:17,217 --> 00:52:19,302
- After you.
- [Awich] <i>See?</i> [laughs]

1115
00:52:19,386 --> 00:52:22,264
- [Nagano] <i>You were right, Awich!</i>
- [Megumi] <i>As expected.</i>

1116
00:52:22,347 --> 00:52:24,099
- [Ari] Have fun.
- [Ma-kun] See you later.

1117
00:52:24,182 --> 00:52:26,685
- [Nagano] <i>She was watching the situation.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Right.</i>

1118
00:52:27,686 --> 00:52:29,187
- [Ma-kun] Shall we go?
- [Ruru] Let's.

1119
00:52:29,271 --> 00:52:30,564
- You like saunas?
- [Ma-kun] I do.

1120
00:52:30,647 --> 00:52:32,232
- [Ruru] Me too.
- They're great, right?

1121
00:52:32,941 --> 00:52:36,361
- Don't cry. [laughing] Don't cry!
- [Ari] Oh, man, this is bad.

1122
00:52:36,444 --> 00:52:38,655
- I'll comfort you.
- Hey, I'm not hurt at all.

1123
00:52:39,239 --> 00:52:42,617
- [Ari] You look like you are.
- I'm not. I'm not hurt at all.

1124
00:52:42,701 --> 00:52:44,661
It's tough
to get your hopes lifted then dropped.

1125
00:52:44,744 --> 00:52:47,289
- [Ari] She approached you.
- [Hikaru] She did? [laughs]

1126
00:52:47,372 --> 00:52:49,249
Yeah, but I thought she'd choose him.

1127
00:52:49,332 --> 00:52:51,251
- [Ari] Oh, really?
- The moment she hesitated.

1128
00:52:53,295 --> 00:52:55,088
REFRESHED

1129
00:52:55,171 --> 00:52:56,673
[exhilarating music playing]

1130
00:52:58,300 --> 00:52:59,968
Wow, this is the best.

1131
00:53:00,719 --> 00:53:03,430
- [Megumi] <i>This time, it's outdoors.</i>
- [Nagamo] <i>Oh!</i>

1132
00:53:03,513 --> 00:53:05,640
<i>- It's so open!</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Yes.</i>

1133
00:53:10,270 --> 00:53:12,689
- Here you are.
- Hey! Wow!

1134
00:53:12,772 --> 00:53:14,190
- Isn't this great?
- It's amazing.

1135
00:53:14,274 --> 00:53:15,108
It's perfect, right?

1136
00:53:15,191 --> 00:53:16,526
[emcees laugh]

1137
00:53:16,610 --> 00:53:18,778
Wait. No, that can't be.

1138
00:53:18,862 --> 00:53:22,157
- Don't you think he has too many tattoos?
- [Nagano] I don't know where to look.

1139
00:53:22,240 --> 00:53:25,076
I mean, he has a Daruma on his stomach.

1140
00:53:26,328 --> 00:53:29,205
- So, why me? Why am I here?
- It's not like that.

1141
00:53:29,289 --> 00:53:30,665
There's a reason for this.

1142
00:53:30,749 --> 00:53:32,792
When we were talking about it
between the girls,

1143
00:53:32,876 --> 00:53:34,294
you were the most popular guy.

1144
00:53:34,878 --> 00:53:37,923
We all agreed on it.
We all agreed that it was you.

1145
00:53:38,006 --> 00:53:38,882
- Seriously?
- Yes.

1146
00:53:38,965 --> 00:53:39,799
Oh, my God.

1147
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:42,510
So, if everyone was
going to give you their letter,

1148
00:53:42,594 --> 00:53:44,512
I thought I should give mine to Leo,

1149
00:53:44,596 --> 00:53:47,349
who was the second guy
I wanted to talk to the most.

1150
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:49,309
- Ah.
- So I gave it to Leo.

1151
00:53:49,392 --> 00:53:51,019
- So that's how it was.
- Yes.

1152
00:53:51,102 --> 00:53:52,103
I see.

1153
00:53:52,187 --> 00:53:54,773
And since we had
this opportunity in the sauna,

1154
00:53:54,856 --> 00:53:56,650
I thought I wanted to talk to you.

1155
00:53:56,733 --> 00:53:59,861
- Oh, I see. Thank you. I see.
- That's why I asked you out.

1156
00:53:59,945 --> 00:54:03,782
She wanted to give it to Ma-kun
but gave it to Leo, her second choice.

1157
00:54:03,865 --> 00:54:05,992
- She says it straight out.
- I know, right?

1158
00:54:06,076 --> 00:54:09,371
I thought you were pretty nice,
and I had a good impression of you.

1159
00:54:09,454 --> 00:54:12,624
I thought you were
the best-looking guy here at first.

1160
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:15,543
- Really?
- [laughs]

1161
00:54:16,127 --> 00:54:20,090
Yeah. I'm saying, right now,
you're the one I'm most interested in.

1162
00:54:20,173 --> 00:54:22,592
Oh, I'm really happy.
I'm so happy to hear that.

1163
00:54:22,676 --> 00:54:25,553
- I wanted to tell you.
- Thank you. I got the message.

1164
00:54:25,637 --> 00:54:28,056
- What do you like? Personality, looks?
- Personality.

1165
00:54:28,139 --> 00:54:29,557
- Personality, huh?
- That's right.

1166
00:54:29,641 --> 00:54:30,475
Oh.

1167
00:54:31,476 --> 00:54:33,311
For what I want, I really think that

1168
00:54:33,395 --> 00:54:36,272
love is more important
than other things, like money.

1169
00:54:36,356 --> 00:54:38,233
- You're a genius.
- [laughs]

1170
00:54:38,316 --> 00:54:40,944
- I'm trying to say all the right things.
- Yeah, you're a genius.

1171
00:54:41,528 --> 00:54:43,571
- Can she really be this nice?
- [laughs]

1172
00:54:44,155 --> 00:54:46,199
But I have my bad side too.

1173
00:54:46,282 --> 00:54:47,450
- Yeah?
- Because I cheat.

1174
00:54:47,534 --> 00:54:49,828
- You're the type that cheats.
- I'm the type that cheats.

1175
00:54:49,911 --> 00:54:52,163
- [groans]
- I'm also telling you my bad side, okay?

1176
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:54,165
- I see.
- Because I was only saying good things.

1177
00:54:54,249 --> 00:54:57,711
- [scoffs]
- I wonder why she chose to say that now.

1178
00:54:57,794 --> 00:54:59,087
What's her plan?

1179
00:54:59,170 --> 00:55:01,297
I think she wants to be loved
for who she is.

1180
00:55:01,381 --> 00:55:02,382
[Megumi and Nagano] Oh!

1181
00:55:02,465 --> 00:55:05,427
I think she's looking for
someone who can do that.

1182
00:55:06,011 --> 00:55:09,222
I mean, I want to have a relationship
where I don't cheat.

1183
00:55:09,305 --> 00:55:12,350
- I really want that. Seriously.
- You're a strong-willed person.

1184
00:55:12,434 --> 00:55:14,394
- Am I strong-willed? Really?
- Yeah, you are. Yeah.

1185
00:55:14,978 --> 00:55:17,313
- Glad to hear that.
- You have a strong sense of self.

1186
00:55:17,397 --> 00:55:18,857
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

1187
00:55:18,940 --> 00:55:20,692
- I like hearing that.
- Isn't that important?

1188
00:55:21,651 --> 00:55:25,238
I really hate it when people say
they'll accept or do something

1189
00:55:25,321 --> 00:55:27,157
even though they don't want to.

1190
00:55:27,240 --> 00:55:28,783
- Mmm.
- Yeah.

1191
00:55:28,867 --> 00:55:32,454
- I'm the type that can't stand that stuff.
- Yeah, uh-huh, uh-huh.

1192
00:55:32,537 --> 00:55:33,788
You gotta have a sense of self.

1193
00:55:33,872 --> 00:55:34,914
- That's right.
- Yeah.

1194
00:55:34,998 --> 00:55:37,167
In the past, for example,

1195
00:55:37,250 --> 00:55:38,460
- with my ex-girlfriend…
- Mmm.

1196
00:55:39,294 --> 00:55:41,671
…I'd say, like,
"Let's have <i>yakiniku</i> to eat."

1197
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:43,173
- I always do, by the way.
- Mmm.

1198
00:55:43,256 --> 00:55:46,885
So, when I told my ex-girlfriend,
she didn't really like <i>yakiniku,</i>

1199
00:55:46,968 --> 00:55:49,763
but she said,
"Oh, that's fine. Anything is fine."

1200
00:55:49,846 --> 00:55:51,306
- I hate that.
- Mmm.

1201
00:55:51,389 --> 00:55:54,476
- She was trying to accommodate me.
- She was kind? Oh. So what would you do?

1202
00:55:54,559 --> 00:55:57,312
Let's say you want to eat <i>yakiniku</i>
but she wants to eat sushi.

1203
00:55:57,395 --> 00:55:59,439
- "Get outta here."
- Oh, you're that type?

1204
00:55:59,522 --> 00:56:01,483
If we're not eating meat,
what's the point?

1205
00:56:01,566 --> 00:56:04,069
- So you're that type of guy.
- A pain in the butt.

1206
00:56:04,152 --> 00:56:07,238
[Nagano] <i>Surprisingly,</i>
<i>we're starting to see Ma-kun's human side.</i>

1207
00:56:07,322 --> 00:56:10,492
- [Megumi] <i>He's like a domineering husband.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Right, exactly.</i>

1208
00:56:11,659 --> 00:56:14,537
So, honestly, how do you feel?
I'm wondering that.

1209
00:56:14,621 --> 00:56:16,498
Huh? Well, it's annoying for one.

1210
00:56:16,581 --> 00:56:18,458
- Annoying? [laughs]
- Yeah.

1211
00:56:19,042 --> 00:56:21,086
- I'm interested in Ma-kun, right?
- Right.

1212
00:56:21,669 --> 00:56:23,588
- And you're interested in Ruru.
- Yeah.

1213
00:56:23,671 --> 00:56:26,049
- And now, those two are there.
- That's why I'm so confused.

1214
00:56:26,132 --> 00:56:28,134
What the heck is she doing? Huh?

1215
00:56:28,718 --> 00:56:30,637
Well, this is going to shake things up.

1216
00:56:31,221 --> 00:56:33,556
I don't know what her intentions are
for choosing him.

1217
00:56:34,390 --> 00:56:37,352
- Are you gonna fight with him?
- Mmm-hmm. If he gets cocky.

1218
00:56:38,770 --> 00:56:41,189
- [Ruru] What? It's beautiful.
- [Ma-kun] Amazing.

1219
00:56:41,272 --> 00:56:43,066
- It's gorgeous.
- It's way too beautiful.

1220
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:46,194
[thrilling music playing]

1221
00:56:51,449 --> 00:56:52,867
[squeals, laughs]

1222
00:56:55,411 --> 00:56:57,580
- You went under. Your hair is wet.
- This feels so good!

1223
00:56:58,164 --> 00:57:00,542
This is the best. Thank you.
This feels so good.

1224
00:57:09,759 --> 00:57:12,720
- [Tai-chan] Wonder what they talked about.
- [Ari] Yeah, I wonder.

1225
00:57:13,888 --> 00:57:16,975
Whatever happened, we should make sure
we all still get along.

1226
00:57:17,058 --> 00:57:17,934
[door opens]

1227
00:57:18,518 --> 00:57:19,936
[Ari] Look. He's grinning so much.

1228
00:57:20,019 --> 00:57:22,147
- [Tai-chan] He's back.
- [Ari] He's grinning.

1229
00:57:24,482 --> 00:57:25,859
- Welcome back.
- [Ma-kun] I'm back.

1230
00:57:25,942 --> 00:57:28,027
- Hey.
- [Ari] Why are you grinning?

1231
00:57:28,111 --> 00:57:29,863
[Ma-kun] I mean, anyone would grin, right?

1232
00:57:30,572 --> 00:57:31,906
Come on, wouldn't you?

1233
00:57:32,699 --> 00:57:34,784
And did you get to know each other?

1234
00:57:35,577 --> 00:57:38,329
[Ma-kun] Well, I won't tell you
what we talked about

1235
00:57:38,413 --> 00:57:39,747
since it involves her too.

1236
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:40,665
Mmm.

1237
00:57:40,748 --> 00:57:43,001
But if you ask me
if I'm interested or not,

1238
00:57:43,084 --> 00:57:44,752
- I would say I'm interested.
- [Ari] Right.

1239
00:57:46,880 --> 00:57:48,214
[Ma-kun] I'm interested in her.

1240
00:57:50,550 --> 00:57:51,968
- [Ruru] I'm back.
- Hey.

1241
00:57:52,051 --> 00:57:53,678
- Welcome back.
- [Assun] How was it?

1242
00:57:53,761 --> 00:57:55,638
- No sauna magic, I'm afraid.
- What?

1243
00:57:55,722 --> 00:57:56,973
- [Ruru laughs]
- [Assun] Why not?

1244
00:57:57,056 --> 00:57:58,892
- [gasps] What?
- [Megumi] Mmm?

1245
00:57:58,975 --> 00:58:00,977
- [Ruru] Well, you know…
- Yeah.

1246
00:58:01,728 --> 00:58:04,856
[Ruru] I thought
Ma-kun seemed a bit mature, you know?

1247
00:58:04,939 --> 00:58:06,608
Like, he seemed calm.

1248
00:58:07,567 --> 00:58:11,988
I was attracted to that,
so I figured I'd ask him out to the sauna.

1249
00:58:12,071 --> 00:58:12,947
[Hikaru] Mmm-hmm.

1250
00:58:13,031 --> 00:58:15,533
But then I thought he was really childish.

1251
00:58:17,327 --> 00:58:18,786
Like… [sighs]

1252
00:58:19,370 --> 00:58:22,332
I'm really disappointed.
He's just a pretty face.

1253
00:58:22,832 --> 00:58:23,958
That's all he has.

1254
00:58:24,918 --> 00:58:27,587
It's awkward to hear you
talk bad about him like that.

1255
00:58:27,670 --> 00:58:28,588
[Maririn] I know.

1256
00:58:28,671 --> 00:58:31,424
- You're supposed to be into each other.
- This is awkward.

1257
00:58:31,925 --> 00:58:33,927
[closing theme song playing]
